[{"id":"pulse-predict-arrive","itemId":"pulse-crossing","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"This is lesson 9.3's <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_cross</code>, with <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_b</code> drawn as the cycles. <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_a</code>, one cycle of the faster <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_a</code>, flips <code class=\"nobreak\">level_a</code> in cycle 0. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_b</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">level_a</code> flips in cycle 0. <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_b</code>'s synchroniser takes the flip at the edges that start cycles 1 and 2, so <code class=\"nobreak\">level_b</code> changes at cycle 2 while <code class=\"nobreak\">last_b</code> still holds the old level: <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_b</code>, their exclusive or, is 1 in cycle 2 alone. At cycle 3, <code class=\"nobreak\">last_b</code> catches up.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"pulse-arrive","source":"hdl/level-09/pulse_cross/pulse_cross_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":33376,"periodText":"33.376 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":6,"signals":[{"label":"clk_b","path":"pulse_cross_tb.clk_b","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"]]},{"label":"pulse_a","path":"pulse_cross_tb.pulse_a","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.687,"1"],[0.9866,"0"],[5.4808,"1"],[5.7804,"0"]]},{"label":"level_a","path":"pulse_cross_tb.dut.level_a","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.8368,"0"],[5.6306,"1"]]},{"label":"pulse_b","path":"pulse_cross_tb.pulse_b","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[2,"1"],[3,"0"]],"samples":["0","0","1","0","0","0"]}]},"answer":"pulse_b","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"pulse-find-bug","itemId":"pulse-crossing","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_cross_bug</code> should carry each one-cycle pulse of <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_a</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_b</code> as one pulse, as lesson 9.3's <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_cross</code> does. Its testbench, the one <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_cross</code> passes, fails: after the first pulse, none has come out. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">level_a</code> should flip at each pulse, <code>level_a ^ pulse_a</code>. As written it takes <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_a</code> itself, one 10 ns cycle of <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_a</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_b</code>'s edges come about every 33 ns, so most pulses fall between two of them and are never seen. A pulse that is caught shows as two changes of <code class=\"nobreak\">level_b</code>, one up and one down, so it comes out twice.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-09/pulse_cross_bug/pulse_cross_bug.sv","firstLine":14,"lines":[[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" level_a;           ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// flips at each pulse_a","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" level_b;           ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// level_a, synchronised to clk_b","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" last_b;            ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// level_b, one edge of clk_b ago","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk_a)","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (rst_a) level_a ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1'b0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"else","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       level_a ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" pulse_a;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"bugLine":20,"fixLine":"else       level_a <= level_a ^ pulse_a;"},{"id":"pulse-fill-change","itemId":"pulse-crossing","role":"core","promptHtml":"In <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_cross</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">level_b</code> is the toggle synchronised to <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_b</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">last_b</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">level_b</code> one edge of <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_b</code> ago. Each pulse of <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_a</code> flips the toggle once, up or down. Fill in <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_b</code>, 1 for one cycle of <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_b</code> after each flip.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>level_b ^ last_b</code> is 1 when the two differ, which is for one cycle after <code class=\"nobreak\">level_b</code> changes, whichever way. Level 4's edge detector, 1 only when the new value is 1 and the old 0, would see only the flips up, and miss every other pulse.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-09/pulse_cross/pulse_cross.sv","firstLine":24,"totalLines":28,"before":["  always_ff @(posedge clk_b)","    last_b <= level_b;",""],"blankLine":{"left":"  assign pulse_b = ","right":";   // a change, either way"},"after":[],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk_b)","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    last_b ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" level_b;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" pulse_b ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":";   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// a change, either way","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}]},"after":[]},"accept":["level_b ^ last_b","last_b ^ level_b"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"What pulse_b is"},{"id":"pulse-report-source","itemId":"pulse-crossing","role":"core","promptHtml":"Below is the one row of <code class=\"nobreak\">press_count_top</code>'s CDC report: the path from the board's clock to <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_b</code>, through <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_cross</code>, whose instance is <code class=\"nobreak\">core/to_b</code>. Source is where the path starts, Destination where it ends.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">level_a_reg</code>, the register of <code class=\"nobreak\">level_a</code>, the toggle, not of <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_a</code>: a pulse never crosses as it is. Its path ends at <code class=\"nobreak\">meta_reg/D</code>, the first flip-flop of <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_cross</code>'s <code class=\"nobreak\">sync2</code>, and nothing else of <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_cross</code> crosses, because <code class=\"nobreak\">pulse_b</code> is made on <code class=\"nobreak\">clk_b</code>'s side.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/press_count/arty-a7-100t/cdc.rpt","firstLine":23,"excerpt":["Row  ID     Severity  Description                                 Depth  Exception            Source (From)            Destination (To)","---  -----  --------  ------------------------------------------  -----  -------------------  -----------------------  -------------------------","  1  CDC-3  Info      1-bit synchronized with ASYNC_REG property      2  Asynch Clock Groups  core/to_b/level_a_reg/C  core/to_b/sync/meta_reg/D"],"ask":"At which register does the path start? Type its name as the report prints it, between core/to_b/ and /C.","answer":"level_a_reg","numeric":false}]